[[:db/retract 17592186059973 :question/answer-fields 17592186056196] {:db/id 17592186059777 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-0a528323-ab00-575c-bdf9-d2b59778522f" "question-c9df2709-22cd-5428-afa6-7b6b2f197bba"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186059778 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-cd94a6c6-a725-5640-bb82-9c092eab6520"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186390017 :question/problem "If $A$ is false and $B$ is false, then $A⇔B$ is" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-0a528323-ab00-575c-bdf9-d2b59778522f" :question/id #uuid "0a528323-ab00-575c-bdf9-d2b59778522f" :question/math-academy-id "q-182535" :question/problem "Find the missing values in the following truth table:" :question/worked-solution "According to the definition of the biconditional, \n\n- $A⇔B$ is true if $A⇒B$ **and** $B⇒A.$ Otherwise, it is false.\n\n- In other words, $A⇔B$ is true if $A$ and $B$ have the same truth values. Otherwise, it is false.\n\nThe complete truth table is shown below:\n\n| $\\,A\\,$ | $\\,B\\,$ | $\\,A⇔B\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ |" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-a79aee92-b4b0-59dd-8a33-6f982f633116" "answer-field-fe0d2b0f-4d76-5461-8f2a-1912cb81b586"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-a79aee92-b4b0-59dd-8a33-6f982f633116" :answer-field/id #uuid "a79aee92-b4b0-59dd-8a33-6f982f633116" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-b78b9fdf-39c3-53bd-acf8-3dcfeb939dba" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d8f2b341-400f-5473-9252-0ed401bbefa9" "answer-b78b9fdf-39c3-53bd-acf8-3dcfeb939dba"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d8f2b341-400f-5473-9252-0ed401bbefa9" :answer/id #uuid "d8f2b341-400f-5473-9