em "Find the missing values in the following truth table:" :question/worked-solution "According to the definition of the biconditional, \n\n- $A⇔B$ is true if $A⇒B$ **and** $B⇒A.$ Otherwise, it is false.\n\n- In other words, $A⇔B$ is true if $A$ and $B$ have the same truth values. Otherwise, it is false.\n\nFirst, we add columns for $¬X$ and $¬X∨Y:$\n\n| $\\,X\\,$ | $\\,Y\\,$ | $\\,¬X\\,$ | $\\,¬X∨Y\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n\nNow, we add a column for $X⇔(¬X∨Y):$\n\n| $\\,X\\,$ | $\\,Y\\,$ | $\\,¬X\\,$ | $\\,¬X∨Y\\,$ | $\\,X⇔(¬X∨Y)\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ |" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f3e75d99-b4ba-522d-8562-a5e96536c6b5" "answer-field-950ec51c-4f09-51f9-9204-de4f2adba147" "answer-field-8e729124-e529-5701-b099-63cd2c843c80" "answer-field-79323a77-92ad-56ee-8252-870e367ebcab"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f3e75d99-b4ba-522d-8562-a5e96536c6b5" :answer-field/id #uuid "f3e75d99-b4ba-522d-8562-a5e96536c6b5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-915ce5ec-5f08-5363-b3ad-6cb09fdb8977" :answer-field/choices ["answer-9f8d15d8-bc6b-5d9f-a27c-6e2871a406dc" "answer-915ce5ec-5f08-5363-b3ad-6cb09fdb8977"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9f8d15d8-bc6b-5d9f-a27c-6e2871a406dc" :answer/id #uuid "9f8d15d8-bc6b-5d9f-a27c-6e2871a406dc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/val